  "id": "Compound::DB06292 - Gene::7363",
  "verbalization": "Dapagliflozin, a sodium-glucose transporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitor, is linked to Ugt2b4 through a series of mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Dapagliflozin, through its class of SGLT2 inhibitors, binds to Ugt2b4, a key enzyme in glucuronidation. This binding is supported by multiple paths, all of which share a common ancestor in the C-Glycosyl Compound and Sglt2 Inhibitor classes, reinforcing the biochemical relationship between the drug and the enzyme. The observed effects, such as vulvitis and recurrent infections, are mediated through the same pathway, indicating that Ugt2b4 may play a role in the pathophysiology of these conditions. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Dapagliflozin influences Ugt2b4, though the exact functional role of Ugt2b4 in these processes remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Dapagliflozin and Ugt2b4, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the biological significance of this interaction.",
